# JavaFX CSS reference checker

Use when the user asks to verify JavaFX CSS rules against official documentation.

## Source of truth

- https://openjfx.io/javadoc/26/javafx.graphics/javafx/scene/doc-files/cssref.html

## Workflow

1. Read the target CSS or inline JavaFX style from the user files.
2. Fetch the JavaFX CSS reference page.
3. Check each requested rule against the reference: selector validity, property name, value syntax, and control-specific scope.
4. Return findings in three blocks: valid, invalid or doubtful, concrete corrections.
5. If the version is ambiguous, ask which JavaFX version to target; default to the reference URL version.

## Output style

- keep answers short and actionable.
- quote the exact CSS fragment when reporting an issue.
- prefer minimal corrections that preserve user intent.
